      "source": [
        "## 1. Real-Life Example & Intuition\n",
        "\n",
        "**Same Problem:**  \n",
        "Predicting customer churn for a telecommunications company.\n",
        "\n",
        "**The AdaBoost Philosophy: \"Learn from Your Mistakes\"**\n",
        "\n",
        "Imagine you're studying for an exam:\n",
        "- **Round 1**: You take a practice test and get some questions wrong\n",
        "- **Round 2**: You focus extra hard on the questions you missed\n",
        "- **Round 3**: You focus even more on the ones that are still tricky\n",
        "- **Final Exam**: You've mastered even the hardest questions\n",
        "\n",
        "**AdaBoost does exactly this:**\n",
        "1. Train a weak model (simple tree)\n",
        "2. Find samples it misclassified\n",
        "3. Give those samples more importance (higher weight)\n",
        "4. Train next model focusing on the hard cases\n",
        "5. Repeat, gradually getting better at difficult examples\n",
        "\n",
        "### AdaBoost vs Random Forest:\n",
        "\n",
        "| Aspect | Random Forest | AdaBoost |\n",
        "|--------|--------------|----------|\n",
        "| **Approach** | Parallel (all trees independent) | Sequential (each tree learns from previous) |\n",
        "| **Focus** | Reduce variance | Reduce bias |\n",
        "| **Tree Training** | Full-depth trees on bootstrap samples | Shallow trees (stumps) on weighted data |\n",
        "| **Diversity** | Random features + bootstrap | Re-weighting misclassified samples |\n",
        "| **Weak Learners** | Strong individual trees | Very weak trees (often just 1-2 levels) |\n",
        "| **Combination** | Simple average/vote | Weighted vote (better trees count more) |\n",
        "| **Sensitivity** | Robust to outliers | Sensitive to noisy data |\n",
        "| **Speed** | Parallelizable | Must be sequential |\n",
        "\n",
        "**Key Insight:**  \n",
        "Random Forest builds many good models independently. AdaBoost builds many weak models that **teach each other**."
      ]
    },
