      "source": [
        "## 2. Algorithm\n",
        "\n",
        "**Initial State:**\n",
        "- All training samples have equal weight: w = 1/N\n",
        "- All samples are equally important\n",
        "\n",
        "**For each iteration t = 1 to T:**\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Train weak classifier** on weighted data\n",
        "   - Simple tree (often just 1 split — called a \"stump\")\n",
        "   - Focuses on currently difficult samples\n",
        "\n",
        "2. **Calculate error rate**\n",
        "   - ε_t = sum of weights of misclassified samples\n",
        "   - If ε_t > 0.5, the classifier is worse than random (stop)\n",
        "\n",
        "3. **Calculate classifier weight**\n",
        "   - α_t = 0.5 * log((1 - ε_t) / ε_t)\n",
        "   - Better classifier (low error) → higher weight\n",
        "   - Worse classifier (high error) → lower weight\n",
        "\n",
        "4. **Update sample weights**\n",
        "   - Misclassified samples: increase weight (focus here next time)\n",
        "   - Correctly classified: decrease weight (less important)\n",
        "   - Formula: w_new = w_old * exp(α_t) if wrong, w_old * exp(-α_t) if correct\n",
        "\n",
        "5. **Normalize weights**\n",
        "   - Ensure all weights sum to 1\n",
        "\n",
        "**Final Prediction:**\n",
        "- Weighted vote: prediction = sign(Σ α_t * h_t(x))\n",
        "- Better models have stronger vote\n",
        "\n",
        "### Visual Intuition:\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "Round 1: ○○○○●●●○○○  (all samples equal weight)\n",
        "         Train → Model 1 (error on ●)\n",
        "         \n",
        "Round 2: ○○○○●●●○○○  (● samples now larger/heavier)\n",
        "         Train → Model 2 (focuses on ●)\n",
        "         \n",
        "Round 3: ○○○○○●○○○○  (remaining hard samples emphasized)\n",
        "         Train → Model 3 (masters the difficult cases)\n",
        "\n",
        "Final:   Weighted vote from all models\n",
        "```"
      ]
    },
